{"chapter": "constructions", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "089R", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$0 < k < n$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathbf{G}(k, n)$", "MATH_0003": "$G(k, n)$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathbf{Z}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathbf{G}(k, n)_S$", "MATH_0006": "$S$", "MATH_0007": "$S$", "MATH_0008": "$R$", "MATH_0009": "$\\Spec(R)$", "MATH_0010": "$\\mathbf{G}(k, n)_R$", "MATH_0011": "$R$", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0002": "}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0003": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it ", "TEXTITOPEN_0002": "{\\it ", "TEXTITOPEN_0003": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-grassmannian}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:d050ed480ce635f0854a659dbba866f69a0e6006136ee4c9e2c86e35b1198396", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:18bfa5c9da84164bd8ffb82e5755781ea5a2ce18e6fc9c01c83984a840c2ab30", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001>. The scheme <MATH_0002> representing the functor\n<MATH_0003> is called <TEXTITOPEN_0001>Grassmannian over <MATH_0004><TEXTITCLOSE_0001>.\nIts base change <MATH_0005> to a scheme <MATH_0006> is called\n<TEXTITOPEN_0002>Grassmannian over <MATH_0007><TEXTITCLOSE_0002>. If <MATH_0008> is a ring the base change\nto <MATH_0009> is denoted <MATH_0010> and called\n<TEXTITOPEN_0003>Grassmannian over <MATH_0011><TEXTITCLOSE_0003>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:96751865528abeca9be9df7ce651f638ca4ff7956d77ec62584fcb114f5a2cfd", "unit_id": "tag:089U:statement"}
{"chapter": "constructions", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "089R", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-gkn-representable}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:25a41b7a59fdea08f4c65f0ef5637c1d23f00c5c4676e6b4b2314f9ef4d39e2a", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThe definition makes sense as we've shown in\nLemma <REF_0001>\nthat these functors are indeed representable.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:379198b5fad4ac16d266eef3a62682137996f47a4d83689ce5ad238ffb67a036", "unit_id": "tag:089R:prose-0002"}
{"chapter": "constructions", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "089R", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$n \\geq 1$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathbf{G}(n, n + 1) = \\mathbf{P}^n_\\mathbf{Z}$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-projective-space-grassmannian}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:83210880b0733e70349b963d34caebb82955f272d5ff91f39a82d90d0f7ffe15", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:72cd0f21822b912d46a2e48929ed6cc0e271f746ff6ddf2dffff6ebd97c3c345", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001>. There is a canonical isomorphism\n<MATH_0002>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:19922dadf1c63ce706c138f116efdbdacdbb536aa44b7a4747dc83b1689d621c", "unit_id": "tag:089V:statement"}
{"chapter": "constructions", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "089R", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathbf{P}^n_\\mathbf{Z}$", "MATH_0002": "$S$", "MATH_0003": "$(\\mathcal{L}, (s_0, \\ldots, s_n))$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{L}$", "MATH_0005": "$(n + 1)$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{L}$", "MATH_0007": "$$\n\\mathcal{O}_S^{\\oplus n + 1} \\longrightarrow \\mathcal{L},\\quad\n(h_0, \\ldots, h_n) \\longmapsto \\sum h_i s_i.\n$$", "MATH_0008": "$q : \\mathcal{O}_S^{\\oplus n + 1} \\to \\mathcal{Q}$", "MATH_0009": "$G(n, n + 1)(S)$", "MATH_0010": "$(\\mathcal{Q}, (q(e_1), \\ldots, q(e_{n + 1})))$", "MATH_0011": "$e_i$", "MATH_0012": "$i = 1, \\ldots, n + 1$", "MATH_0013": "$\\mathcal{O}_S^{\\oplus n + 1}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-projective-space}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:6d09428becab43f1d4371b1be7aaca38b052dcb44f7fc097d41af667571c639d", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:83680c7ebb96a70f0549b7951011d0b6c9872d3c0c94f0b7ff7bab6871bddee2", "source_text": "According to Lemma <REF_0001> the scheme\n<MATH_0001> represents the functor\nwhich assigns to a scheme <MATH_0002> the set of isomorphisms classes\nof pairs <MATH_0003> consisting of\nan invertible module <MATH_0004> and an <MATH_0005>-tuple\nof global sections generating <MATH_0006>.\nGiven such a pair we obtain a quotient\n<MATH_0007>\nConversely, given an element\n<MATH_0008> of <MATH_0009>\nwe obtain such a pair, namely <MATH_0010>.\nHere <MATH_0011>, <MATH_0012> are the standard generating sections\nof the free module <MATH_0013>.\nWe omit the verification that these constructions define mutually\ninverse transformations of functors.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:63905d7333d388def043f849d75210162ed0d0dc021ad9113199eb23d76918db", "unit_id": "tag:089V:proof"}
